# ─── Local development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With nothing set below, the app runs fully locally:
#   database -> PGlite (PostgreSQL 18 compiled to WASM) in ./.pglite
#   images   -> public/uploads
# No Docker, no Postgres install, no cloud account required.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ─── Supabase: database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set DATABASE_URL and the app switches from PGlite to Supabase Postgres.
# Use the TRANSACTION POOLER string (port 6543) from
#   Supabase -> Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string -> Transaction pooler
# Serverless functions need the pooler, not the direct 5432 connection.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres


# ─── Supabase: image storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set both and listing photos move from public/uploads to Supabase Storage.
# Create a PUBLIC bucket named `listings` first: Storage -> New bucket -> Public.
# The service role key bypasses all row-level security. Keep it server-side only:
# never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit it.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role-key>
# SUPABASE_BUCKET=listings


# ─── Lead notification e-mail (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Without these the enquiry still lands in /admin/erdeklodesek — you just do not get
# an e-mail about it. Sign up at resend.com, verify the sending domain, then:
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# LEAD_NOTIFY_FROM=Oli Felni <noreply@olifelni.com>   # must be on the verified domain
# LEAD_NOTIFY_TO=olifelni5@gmail.com                   # comma-separated for several


# ─── Production ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://olifelni.com
